  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ndpi_search_fix",
    "file": "ndpi/src/lib/protocols/fix.c",
    "description": "ndpi_search_fix performs fixed-offset payload signature checks (payload[0]..payload[5]) without first validating packet->payload_packet_len >= 6. For short TCP payloads, the code reads past the end of the heap buffer, causing the ASan heap-buffer-overflow at fix.c:38.",
    "conditions": "In fuzz_process_packet, attacker-controlled input is passed directly to ndpi_detection_process_packet, which may classify it as a TCP flow with nonzero payload and invoke FIX detection via check_ndpi_tcp_flow_func. If the payload is shorter than 6 bytes (or otherwise not guaranteed to contain all accessed offsets), ndpi_search_fix still dereferences payload[0..5], triggering an out-of-bounds read."
  },
